/** @page pdfreleasenotes Release Notes

    @section pdf_1_0_0 pdf Module Version 1.0.0
    - initial release
    - a custom font file (the \c font_path of a font) that the calling code gives
      @ref Qore::Pdf::PdfEditor::drawText() "PdfEditor::drawText()" is refused with \c PERMISSION-DENIED if that
      code is restricted from the file system, and the file-system policy of a sandbox that governs the code applies
      to it (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/module-pdf/issues/8">issue 8</a>)
    - @ref Qore::Pdf::PdfDocument::split() "PdfDocument::split()" checks each output file with the file-system
      policy of a sandbox that governs the calling code, as the prefix can name another directory
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/module-pdf/issues/8">issue 8</a>)
    - the file paths that the methods of the PDF classes take, and the \c font_path of a font, are refused with
      \c PERMISSION-DENIED for the restricted code that a host-created object of a module class was given to, as
      the object's methods run with the file system lent (see @ref pdfcallerpaths and
      @ref Qore::Pdf::PDF_LENT_PATH_CHECKS,
      <a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/module-pdf/issues/12">issue 12</a>)
    - @ref Qore::Pdf::PdfEditor::getEncryptionInfoFromData() "PdfEditor::getEncryptionInfoFromData()" returns the
      encryption information of a document in memory
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/module-pdf/issues/10">issue 10</a>)
    - a @ref Qore::Pdf::PdfEditor "PdfEditor" created from data keeps the data that it reads its objects from later;
      it read released memory once the caller released the data
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/module-pdf/issues/13">issue 13</a>)
*/
